error[E0405]: `f` holds a resource (`File`), which can't be put in a cown
  --> cown_resource.ck:10:11
   |
10 | fn direct f s -> c : f~File, s~Sched, c~Cown File
   |           ^
   = note: `f` is passed to `cown.new`; a cown's handle can be shared, so nothing would make sure what it holds is closed (D156)
   = help: keep the resource with one owner, passing it on through calls, `fork` and `join`; a cown may hold the rest of the state

error[E0405]: `f` holds a resource (`File`), which can't be put in a cown
  --> cown_resource.ck:17:11
   |
17 | fn inside f s -> c : f~File, s~Sched, c~Cown Job
   |           ^
   = note: `f` is passed to `cown.new`; a cown's handle can be shared, so nothing would make sure what it holds is closed (D156)
   = help: keep the resource with one owner, passing it on through calls, `fork` and `join`; a cown may hold the rest of the state

error[E0405]: `v` is `own`, so it may be a resource, which can't be put in a cown
  --> cown_resource.ck:20:12
   |
20 | fn generic v s -> c : v~own a, s~Sched, c~Cown a
   |            ^
   = help: remove `own`: a cown holds only values that aren't resources (D156)

error[E0405]: `f` holds a resource (`File`), which can't be put in an actor's state
  --> cown_resource.ck:23:10
   |
23 | fn state f s -> a : f~File, s~Sched, a~Actor (Option File)
   |          ^
   = note: `f` is passed to `actor.new`; a cown's handle can be shared, so nothing would make sure what it holds is closed (D156)
   = help: keep the resource with one owner, passing it on through calls, `fork` and `join`; a cown may hold the rest of the state

